  "problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}?$\n\n- $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=7$ $$\n- $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x+2=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x$ $$\n- $7\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=-5$",
  "worked_solution": "We first simplify the given equations, and get\n\n- $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=7$ $$\n- $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$\n- $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=-\\frac{5}{7}$\n\nNow, recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solutions.",
